shape theory.dimension.handedness : theory.dimension.chirality, theory.coherence.law2, theory.minimal {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 8.7 (Chiral Handedness).
// Every chiral loop has two orientations (handednesses).
// Conservation (Law 2) requires both to exist with equal
// structural weight.
//
// A chiral loop traverses generators in sequence: X -> Y -> Z.
// The same loop in reverse (Z -> Y -> X) is a distinct orientation.
// If only one handedness existed, that would be structural content
// appearing from nothing, violating Law 2.
//
// Corollary 8.8 (Achiral Origin): empty_s has no handedness.
// It has no distinguishing character, no chiral loop, no orientation.
// empty_s is the achiral center.
//
// Corollary 8.9 (Chiral Symmetry from Conservation):
// Moment sequences emerging from empty_s exist in complementary
// chiral pairs. For every sequence with one handedness, a
// complementary sequence with the opposite handedness exists with
// equal structural weight.
//
// Derives from: theory.dimension.chirality, theory.coherence.law2,
//               theory.minimal
  """
}
